.TH tensor-wasm-metrics 1  "tensor-wasm-metrics "
.SH NAME
tensor\-wasm\-metrics \- Fetch and pretty\-print Prometheus metrics from a TensorWasm server
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtensor\-wasm metrics\fR \fB\-\-server\fR=\fISERVER\fR [\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Issues \fBGET {server}/metrics\fR and prints the response body verbatim. Prometheus text exposition is plain UTF\-8 by design, so no extra formatting is applied. A non\-2xx response is rendered through the shared error\-envelope helper and the process exits non\-zero.
.PP
Pipe to \fBgrep '^tensor_wasm_'\fR to filter to TensorWasm's own series.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR=\fISERVER\fR
Base URL of the target TensorWasm server (e.g. \fBhttp://localhost:8080\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR [default: 0]
Tenant id to advertise on outbound API requests.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBTENSOR_WASM_TOKEN\fR
Bearer token attached as \fBAuthorization: Bearer ...\fR on the outbound request when set.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tensor\-wasm(1), tensor\-wasm\-observe(1)
